+| AC-011 | Invitation acceptance | A valid controlled recipient can accept and receive only the intended store/role; existing/new identities follow the approved identity policy. | D-02 | Actual email/inbox and browser proof for both identity cases |
+| AC-012 | Invitation abuse | Expired/revoked/replayed/altered invitations fail safely; link GET does not redeem, explicit button POST does. Wrong-user acceptance requires deliberate identity switching; altered account/store targets are denied. Opening the emailed link (GET) does not accept the invitation; only the explicit action (POST) does. | D-02 | Token and browser negative coverage |
+| AC-013 | Resend and revoke | Resends, duplicates and revocation obey explicit token validity, delivery and dedupe rules; old links cannot revive revoked authority. | D-02 | Delivery counters and link-state tests |
+| AC-014 | Admin replacement | Owner-controlled replacement keeps the incumbent admin until the replacement accepts and preserves exactly one effective admin per active store through acceptance, concurrency, expiration and failure. | D-02 | Database concurrency and two-identity browser journey |
+| AC-015 | Member revocation | Authorized removal ends store access at application and data layers while preserving records; test already-issued direct tokens and measure/state any residual against the frozen policy rather than silently accepting it. | D-02 | Fresh and existing-session tests plus direct API checks |
+| AC-016 | Last-admin protection | Self-removal or conflicting role changes cannot orphan an active store; the approved owner/support recovery remains possible. | D-02,D-04 | Concurrency, denial and recovery proof |
+| AC-017 | Tenant and role isolation | Owner/admin/member/unrelated-owner checks cover both apps and protected fields; invitation or handoff grants no extra billing or cross-tenant rights. | D-02 | Independent role-by-route/API/DB matrix |
+| AC-018 | Scheduled removal | Named-store removal takes effect at the approved paid-period boundary; access and quantity change coherently, records remain, and repeat jobs/events are safe. | D-03 | Controlled time/event and provider/local evidence |
+| AC-019 | Removal undo | Undo is allowed before the paid period ends; the frozen cutoff semantics are enforced before/at/after that boundary; pending add/remove/renewal changes cannot silently overcharge or reactivate a store. | D-03 | Boundary and concurrency tests |
